        "comments": "The assembly ddSalRepe1.hap2.1 is based on 33x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Hap1:Chromosome Z was identified through synteny analysis with Salix viminalis (GCA_029228465.1)The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 5 (5,500 - 11,300 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 7 (16,400 - 19,221 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 8 (10,550 - 11,000 Kbp) are unknown.Hap2:The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 6 (6,050 - 11,400 Kbp) are unknown.",
